---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Nora Casey — a trans woman from Seattle, living in Barcelona, writing short fiction, essays and the occasional poem."
>
  <article class="max-w-2xl mx-auto prose-reader">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)] leading-tight mb-6">
      About
    </h1>

    <p>
      I’m Nora — a trans woman from Seattle, living in Barcelona. I write short fiction, essays and
      the occasional poem. Some of it is true. Some of it is about a competitive eater named Jim.
    </p>

    <p>
      My days are spent in the sun, in community with friends and chosen family. I explore beautiful
      architecture with my eyes and a camera, eat my way through a maze of Latin, Asian and
      Mediterranean food, and find ways to make street signs look queer. I talk to strangers. I
      write my phone number in books and then donate them. I like the kind of risk where the odds
      aren’t purely mathematical — where if it works out, the only available explanation is fate.
    </p>

    <p>
      This is where I put the writing I want in the world. If something here lands, tell me. I’m a
      parasite when it comes to compliments from strangers.
    </p>

    {/* "Reach me at" and the link share a line on purpose. The build compresses
        HTML with JSX whitespace rules, which drop the line break between a run of
        text and an inline element beside it — split over two lines this renders as
        "Reach me athello@novellanora.com". Whitespace WITHIN a line is kept, which
        is the whole of why this one survives. A JSX comment rather than an HTML
        one: a note about the build is not something to serve to a reader. */}
    <p>
      Reach me at <a href="mailto:hello@novellanora.com">hello@novellanora.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
